      "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nEnabled chunked prefill and prefix caching on RISC-V CPUs.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Chunked prefill and prefix caching are enabled on RISC-V CPUs.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nTested on main @ f98ae6a9fd + this change under QEMU (qemu-riscv64 11.0.2, RVV VLEN 128, attention ISA `rvv`) with `meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct`, `block_size=32`, `max_num_batched_tokens=32`, on three greedy prompts (79/79/78 tokens; prompts 2 and 3 share a 64+-token prefix and run in that order):\r\n\r\n- Chunked prefill acted: prompts 1 and 2 were scheduled as 32 + 32 + 15 tokens per step (`SchedulerOutput.num_scheduled_tokens`); main schedules each in one 79-token step.\r\n- Prefix caching acted: prompt 3 reported `num_cached_tokens=64` (two 32-token blocks matched by block hash) and computed the remaining 14 tokens in one step; main reports 0.\r\n- The generated token ids equal main's on all three prompts, with the features off and on.\r\n\r\nKernel test, same build under QEMU: `pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_cpu_attn.py -k \"normal_rvv and (seq_lens1 or seq_lens2) and dtype2 and auto\"` → 72 passed\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nNot a duplicate: no open PR or issue covers this.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, 